        "description": null,
        "body": "# API REV 004 Research Checkpoint\n\n**Brief Title:** API REV 004 live team 2026-07-29T13:59:06.106Z\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- API revision 004 represents the fourth major iteration in the universal application framework proposal, building on established patterns from REV 001-003\n- Current live team deployment requires stability focus; breaking changes must be carefully evaluated against existing integrations\n- Importable package structure in brief-studio/dist supports modular API distribution with clear versioning boundaries\n- Version 004 introduces compatibility layers that enable gradual migration from REV 003 without forced immediate upgrades\n- Test coverage requirements have increased to 95% minimum for all public API surface areas in this revision\n\n## Risks & Open Questions\n\n- Migration path complexity: teams using REV 002 directly may face multi-step upgrade challenges; need to validate skip-generation compatibility\n- Documentation synchronization: API spec updates must stay aligned with implementation; risk of drift during parallel development cycles\n- Backward compatibility guarantees undefined for edge cases in legacy authentication flows; requires explicit policy decision\n\n## Recommendations & Next Steps\n\n- Prioritize non-breaking changes for REV 004; defer structural refactors to REV 005\n- Create migration guide documenting upgrade paths from REV 002, 003, and direct 004 adoption\n- Establish API deprecation timeline (minimum 2 revision cycles) for any sunset features in this release\n- Coordinate with writer to produce implementation brief covering: change summary, migration instructions, and compatibility matrix\n",
        "producerMemberRouteKey": "researcher",
        "updatedAt": "2026-07-29T14:02:54.053Z"
