        "description": "API REV 004 implementation brief with migration guidance and risk assessment",
        "body": "# API REV 004 Implementation Brief\n\n## Recommendation Summary\n\nProceed with API REV 004 as a stability-focused release that maintains backward compatibility with REV 002-003 while introducing compatibility layers for gradual migration. Defer any structural refactors to REV 005 and enforce a minimum 95% test coverage requirement across the public API surface. This approach balances the need for new features with deployment safety for existing integrations.\n\n## Key Evidence\n\n- REV 004 builds on established patterns from prior revisions (REV 001-003), providing a mature foundation for incremental improvements\n- Compatibility layers enable teams to migrate from REV 003 without forced immediate upgrades, reducing deployment risk\n- Importable package structure in `brief-studio/dist` supports clear versioning boundaries for modular API distribution\n- Current live team deployment context requires careful evaluation of breaking changes against existing integrations\n\n## Risks & Cautions\n\n- Multi-step upgrade complexity: Teams skipping from REV 002 directly to REV 004 may encounter untested migration paths\n- Documentation drift risk: API spec updates must stay synchronized with implementation during parallel development cycles\n- Legacy authentication flows have undefined backward compatibility guarantees; requires explicit policy decision before release\n\n## Next Actions\n\n- Produce migration guide documenting upgrade paths from REV 002, REV 003, and direct REV 004 adoption scenarios\n- Establish explicit API deprecation timeline (minimum 2 revision cycles) for any sunset features in this release\n- Validate skip-generation compatibility by testing REV 002 → REV 004 upgrade path\n- Finalize implementation brief with change summary and compatibility matrix for stakeholder review\n",
        "producerMemberRouteKey": "writer",
